A||N||3||fropuff||They've gone too far!!!||||10||
Z||000000||fropuff||06-15-2000||09:26 AM||||Hey, I don't know if anyone watched last night's Tonight Show w/ Jay Leno, but I thought I'd fill you in.  There again, was a poor, defenseless, little red Fiero (probably the same onw as last week).  Only this time, they totaled the whole frickin' car.  Last time was a wall of bricks falling on the front end, smashing the windshield, probably had some spare parts on hand, but this time, they ran the poor, little, red Fiero over with a tank.  This just kinda made me mad.  It was probably the same car as last week, just fixed, but I'm still mad.  I don't know how Jay can let anyone purposely wreck an American legend (well, I don't know if it goes that far.) I think we should go down to Burbank and steal their "joy Fiero" before anything else happens to it.  Oh, for those who want to know what the scene was:  (It's gonna get long here.  Might want to take a bathroom break.).......There's something they call "Ask Jay Anything".  Well, there was this guy that told him it looked like he drives a new, different car to the studio every day.  Jay said yes, but they're also old cars.  More than 50 years old.  He also added that he parks them in a way that he cannot be "doored" by other cars.  Then Edd Hall, his producer, interrupted and said Jay is usually the one dinging.  Jay said, "no, well that today was an accident.  All it caused was a small ding."  Edd: "No, it was a dent."  Jay: "No, it wasn't!  It was a ding."  Edd: "Well, we have security footage of the whole thing".  Then they have a closeup where Edd is polishing off an area of the roof panel.  Then they pan out,  Holy Crap! a Fiero!  It was an 84 coupe, red, tan interior, same as last time.  Anyway, then Jay comes driving in with his tank, runs over the poor, little Fiero, and says to Edd: "Sorry."  Oh man.   ||||reg||10
Z||000001||fropuff||06-15-2000||09:28 AM||||By the way, the tank ran over the entire front end of the car up to about the rear deck.  There's no way this Fiero's getting out of it.  Don't be expecting a red 84 coupe with a tan interior to be on soon. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||ChadMan||06-15-2000||11:20 AM||||As much as I hate to see Fieros disrespected, a little part of me is glad, because it keeps the prices down.<P>There are lots of cool classic cars I'd like to have - an MGB, an Alfa Romeo Graduate, a late 60's/early 70's Porsche 911 (or even a 914), a Corvette of any year, a 65 or 66 Mustang, an Austin/Healey Sprite...  It seems only the Fiero is affordable, thanks to its undeserved bad reputation.<P>Let the snobs congregate at Monterey.  We'll be in Louisville having a great time.  Crush away, Jay - we'll have the last laugh.||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||06-15-2000||04:09 PM||||Yeah this place it full of snobs this week.  Limo's everywhere.  I wish they'd stay the hell out of my way.  I hate seeing these tourists reading maps while drive 5 mph down the road.  I'm getting OUT of town this weekend.  Going to cruise the GT up to Sacramento to enjoy some hot weather by the river. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> AWAY from the tourists.||||reg||1
